Yes, totally possible – you’re already producing great data, you just need a proper TUI (terminal UI) instead of wall-of-text println!.

There are basically two levels you can go for:

Quick win: colored, slightly formatted text (minimal refactor).

Real dashboard: panels, mini-charts, live updates with a TUI crate.

I’ll show both.

1. Quick win: color + formatting with minimal change
Use a color crate and keep your current logging structure.

a) Add a color crate
In Cargo.toml:

[dependencies]
owo-colors = "4"
b) Wrap your printing in a small helper
Example (pseudo‐metrics struct):

use owo_colors::OwoColorize;

pub struct CoreMetrics {
    pub mid: f64,
    pub micro: f64,
    pub spread: f64,
    pub bid: f64,
    pub ask: f64,
    pub imb: f64,
    pub pwi_1: f64,
    pub pwi_5: f64,
    pub pwi_25: f64,
    pub pwi_50: f64,
}

pub fn print_core_metrics(m: &CoreMetrics) {
    println!(
        "{} {} | {}",
        "[CORE]".bright_blue().bold(),
        "MID/MICRO/SPRD".bold(),
        chrono::Utc::now().to_rfc3339().dimmed()
    );

    println!(
        "  MID:   {} | MICRO: {} ({}) | SPRD: {}",
        format!("{:.4}", m.mid).yellow(),
        format!("{:.4}", m.micro).yellow(),
        format!("Δ {:+.4}", m.micro - m.mid)
            .if_then(m.micro >= m.mid, |s| s.green())
            .if_then(m.micro < m.mid, |s| s.red()),
        format!("{:.4}", m.spread).cyan()
    );

    println!(
        "  BID/ASK: {}/{} | IMB: {}",
        format!("{:.4}", m.bid).green(),
        format!("{:.4}", m.ask).red(),
        format!("{:.2}%", m.imb * 100.0).magenta()
    );

    println!(
        "  PWI: 1%={} 5%={} 25%={} 50%={}",
        fmt_pwi(m.pwi_1),
        fmt_pwi(m.pwi_5),
        fmt_pwi(m.pwi_25),
        fmt_pwi(m.pwi_50),
    );
    println!();
}

fn fmt_pwi(v: f64) -> String {
    use owo_colors::OwoColorize;
    let pct = v * 100.0;
    let s = format!("{:+.2}%", pct);
    if pct > 5.0 {
        s.green().to_string()
    } else if pct < -5.0 {
        s.red().to_string()
    } else {
        s.dimmed().to_string()
    }
}

// small helper extension
trait IfThenStyle: Sized {
    fn if_then<F>(self, cond: bool, f: F) -> Self
    where
        F: FnOnce(Self) -> Self;
}

impl<T> IfThenStyle for T {
    fn if_then<F>(self, cond: bool, f: F) -> Self
    where
        F: FnOnce(Self) -> Self,
    {
        if cond { f(self) } else { self }
    }
}
